  "proposal_rule": "Project the selected stable instance vertices with evaluator-authoritative pose and intrinsics, take the frozen tight bounding box, crop raw RGB, then square-pad the shorter dimension with black. The 32-pixel frame margin is fixed before RGB from the SceneNN edge-clipping falsifier.",
  "claim_boundary": "A pass is a small real-image Development canary that the frozen same-point appearance lock transfers from outdoor 3D Street View to truth-proposed stable indoor 3RScan door or doorframe instances. 3RScan mesh, pose, depth, RGB and semantic labels come from one provider; target triples are disjoint from the four enumerated prior cohorts, but up to two targets may share one reference scan and scan families may have appeared in prior Development; proposals use privileged reconstructed geometry; and only three physical targets are tested. It is not door detection, pixel-mask transfer, doorway aperture, named entrance, venue ownership, public access, traversability, approach waypoint, arrival, HANDOFF_READY, open-world or provider-independent confirmation, user benefit or mobility-safety evidence."
